            <ArticleTitle>Pleomorphic xanthoastrocytoma of the pineal region.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1439-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jocn.2010.02.022</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pleomorphic xanthoastrocytomas are indolent, astrocytic tumors usually located in the superficial cerebral cortex. They have not been described as occurring in the pineal region. We describe a patient with an astrocytic tumor arising in the pineal region that fulfilled all of the morphologic and immunohistochemical criteria of a pleomorphic xanthoastrocytoma. To our knowledge, this is the first description of a pleomorphic xanthoastrocytoma located in the pineal region.</AbstractText>
